<title>USA: Fed's Rivlin says dollar may not get much stronger.</title>
<headline>Fed's Rivlin says dollar may not get much stronger.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve vice chairwoman Alice Rivlin said on Wednesday the strength of the U.S. dollar had helped to keep import prices in check but that the currency was unlikely to race ahead much further.</p>
<p>&quot;The dollar may not get much stronger but it certainly has helped to keep import prices down,&quot; she told the House Banking committee in testimony.</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8300))</p>
